<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31105" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nōdo</span></b> , āvi, ātum,
		1, v. a.
		nodus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to furnish</i> or <i>fill with knots</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferula nodata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 22, 42, § 123</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornus nodata,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 38, 73, § 186</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to tie in a knot,
				to knot</i>, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 32, 2</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crines nodantur in aurum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 138</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">collum laqueo nodatus ab arto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animalia phalerari sibi magis quam nodari
					videntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. in Cant. Cantic. 1, §
				43</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nōdātus</span></b> , a, um, <i>P. a., knotty</i>, i. e. <i>entangled,
				intricate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rapidus nodato gurgite vortex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 9, 276</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
